   "id": 334803,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Before the Industrial revolution light-colored moths were able to blend in with the environment and better avoid predators. Since the Industrial Revolution, dark-colored moths are better camouflaged than light-colored moths. The number of dark-colored moths has increased to be the most common color. This is an example of what?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 844830,
     "content_html": "directional selection"
    },
    {
     "id": 844827,
     "content_html": "stabilizing selection"
    },
    {
     "id": 844828,
     "content_html": "frequency-dependent selection"
    },
    {
     "id": 844829,
     "content_html": "diversifying selection"
    }
   ],
